Re: YO input data files

From:  Roger Cox - Telex/Hy-Gain, Lincoln, NE  14 Apr 1998


  The files on this disk are input data files meant to be
used with the program - Yagi Optimizer by Brian Beezley K6STI.
The files that end with "YAG" may be used with Yagi Optimizer
Version 4, 5 or 6. 

These files represent Hy-Gain single-band Yagi antennas
for the 20,17,15,12, and 10 meter bands.  The "BA" antennas
are older designs and the YO-models may or may not have been
verified. The "CA" antennas have been designed using YO and
have been completely verified on Hy-Gain's antenna test
range.  The VSWR of our antennas have been measured using
Hewlitt-Packard Network Analyzers models 8505 and 8752A. The
radiation patterns were measured using an 80 foot rotating
pole and Scientific Atlanta model 1530 polar recorder.(see
page 46 February 1985 QST)

   The numbers on the end of each file indicate the setting
of each model, e.g. HG155CA1 indicates that this file is the
Hy-Gain model 155CA setting number 1.  Usually, setting
number 1 will be the lowest setting or the CW setting.

   The YO input data files should be complete with
information on all available settings as of this date.  The
YS input data files represent one setting for each model.
You may create the files for the other settings, if you wish.
We have many more settings for these antennas that are
considered experimental at this time.  That is, we have
modeled the antennas with YO and YS, but we have not yet
verified the performance on our range.  Some of these are
maximum gain, maximum F/B and broad-band settings.  These
experimental settings are not included om this disk, however
if you are interested in trying one of these, please let me
know.

   The 105CA files were updated on July 26, 1993, as the 105BA-S 
has been replaced now with the 105CA.  The 105CA contains the same
parts as the 105BA-S, however it has 7 standard settings.

